
1. What is CSS Grid?
CSS Grid is a two-dimensional CSS layout system used
to arrange webpage elements in rows and columns.
It helps create organized and responsive layouts.

2. Difference between Flexbox and Grid?
Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system used to
arrange elements in a single row or column, whereas
CSS Grid is a two-dimensional layout system used
to arrange elements in both rows and columns.

3. What is the purpose of grid-template-columns?
grid-template-columns is used to define the number
and size of columns in a grid container.

4. Why do we use media queries?
Media queries are used to apply different CSS styles
according to screen sizes and device characteristics.
They help make websites responsive on desktops,
tablets and mobile devices.